{
  "facts": [
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh Morris is the mother of a 12-day-old infant named Ruby.",
      "cites": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The health visitor is Bethan Lloyd.",
      "cites": [
        1
      ],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The visit is a new birth visit for Ruby, who is 12 days old.",
      "cites": [
        5
      ],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh is breastfeeding Ruby primarily, with one bottle of formula given at night.",
      "cites": [
        10
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ruby is fed every two to two and a half hours during the day, with occasional cluster feeding.",
      "cites": [
        12
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ruby has six to seven wet nappies per day.",
      "cites": [
        14
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ruby's birth weight was 3.2 kg as recorded by the midwife on day five.",
      "cites": [
        15
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ruby's current weight is 3.41 kg, measured at the time of the visit.",
      "cites": [
        61
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh reports that her physical recovery postpartum is 'bit sore still but better'.",
      "cites": [
        16
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh reports that her mood is 'up and down' and that she 'cries a lot'.",
      "cites": [
        18
      ],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh's partner, Dean, is at work during the visit and returns around 3 PM.",
      "cites": [
        20
      ],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dean works early shifts at a warehouse.",
      "cites": [
        20
      ],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh and Dean have a tense relationship due to lack of sleep.",
      "cites": [
        22
      ],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dean pushed Kayleigh into a wardrobe door during an argument, which occurred three to four times since summer.",
      "cites": [
        26,
        28
      ],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dean punched Kayleigh in the stomach during pregnancy in August, at approximately 30 weeks gestation.",
      "cites": [
        34,
        36,
        38
      ],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh did not report any further physical harm from Dean during pregnancy.",
      "cites": [
        38
      ],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dean checks Kayleigh's phone every night and goes mad if she messages someone he does not like.",
      "cites": [
        40,
        42
      ],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh has not seen her mother since September, before Ruby was born.",
      "cites": [
        44,
        46
      ],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh's mother has not met Ruby.",
      "cites": [
        46
      ],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dean has never hurt or been rough with Ruby.",
      "cites": [
        48
      ],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh feels safe at home during the visit because Dean is at work.",
      "cites": [
        50
      ],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh is willing to receive a referral to Harbridge Women's Aid, an outreach service, which will call her sister Kirsty's number when Dean is at work.",
      "cites": [
        51,
        52,
        53,
        54
      ],
      "section": "Support network and finances"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh will provide the number 077 for the outreach service to use.",
      "cites": [
        70
      ],
      "section": "Support network and finances"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh has applied for child benefit but does not currently have her own bank card.",
      "cites": [
        66
      ],
      "section": "Support network and finances"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh registered Ruby's birth on the day before the visit.",
      "cites": [
        68
      ],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kayleigh's GP, Dr Anand, will be informed about the safeguarding concerns.",
      "cites": [
        73
      ],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "The health visitor will refer Kayleigh to Harbridge Women's Aid and the referral will be made on the same day.",
      "cites": [
        71
      ],
      "section": "Agreed actions"
    },
    {
      "text": "The outreach service will call Kayleigh's sister Kirsty's phone by Friday.",
      "cites": [
        71
      ],
      "section": "Agreed actions"
    },
    {
      "text": "The health visitor will speak to the safeguarding lead and inform the GP about the concerns on the same day.",
      "cites": [
        73
      ],
      "section": "Agreed actions"
    },
    {
      "text": "The health visitor will return on Thursday, 3rd December, at 11 AM when Dean is at work.",
      "cites": [
        75
      ],
      "section": "Agreed actions"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "facts": [
    {
      "text": "Dennis Walsh (Mr Walsh) is the person being assessed.",
      "cites": [1, 2],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Karen Walsh is the daughter of Dennis Walsh and is present during the assessment.",
      "cites": [3, 4, 5],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The purpose of the visit is a six-month review of the care package.",
      "cites": [4],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The care assessor, Priya Nair, will be writing notes during the assessment.",
      "cites": [6],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The assessor will not share information with the council unless there is a safeguarding concern, and will inform the person first.",
      "cites": [6],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Brightpath Home Care currently visits Mr Walsh four times a day.",
      "cites": [8, 9],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "The four visits occur in the morning, at dinner, at tea, and at bedtime.",
      "cites": [9],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh reports that some carers are good, and specifically praises Shelley, the teatime carer, for taking her time.",
      "cites": [11],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh cannot button his clothes due to hand difficulties.",
      "cites": [13],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh does not go up the stairs and sleeps downstairs.",
      "cites": [13],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "The bed was brought down in March after a fall.",
      "cites": [14],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh uses the frame around the house most of the time, when he remembers.",
      "cites": [16],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carers prepare microwave meals for dinner and tea.",
      "cites": [18],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Karen brings a proper dinner round on Sundays.",
      "cites": [18],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carers prompt Mr Walsh's diabetes tablets at morning and night.",
      "cites": [20],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh reports that Lee, the morning carer, is always in a rush.",
      "cites": [22],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh states that Lee slapped him across the face with an open hand.",
      "cites": [26, 30],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh reports that Lee slapped him twice: once last Thursday and once a few weeks back, both times because he was slow getting off the bed.",
      "cites": [26, 28],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh reports that Lee grabbed his left arm to pull him up from the commode, and that this happened most mornings when it was Lee.",
      "cites": [24, 32, 34, 36],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh reports that Lee grabbed his arm hard on Saturday, which 'really hurt'.",
      "cites": [34],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Karen Walsh discovered bruises on Mr Walsh's left upper arm when she helped him change his top on Sunday.",
      "cites": [39],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "The bruises were four in a row, like fingermarks, on the inside of the upper arm, and were purple.",
      "cites": [41],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Karen took photos of the bruises on her phone on Sunday.",
      "cites": [41],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Karen asked her father about the bruises and he initially said he'd knocked it, then told her about Lee the previous night.",
      "cites": [43],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh said he did not want a fuss and did not want to lose the carers.",
      "cites": [44],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh has not told anyone at Brightpath about the incidents with Lee.",
      "cites": [52],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh wants Lee to stop coming to him and wants someone like Shelley to replace him.",
      "cites": [54],
      "section": "Person's views and wishes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh used to go to the bowls club but has not attended since his hip injury.",
      "cites": [58],
      "section": "Person's views and wishes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Karen Walsh is responsible for shopping for her father using his card and keeps the receipts.",
      "cites": [56],
      "section": "Support network and finances"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mr Walsh receives the higher rate of Attendance Allowance.",
      "cites": [55],
      "section": "Support network and finances"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "facts": [
    {
      "text": "Tom Ashworth is the social worker.",
      "cites": [1],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie Rowe is the person being assessed.",
      "cites": [2],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The assessment is scheduled as a review, as previously discussed.",
      "cites": [5],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The social worker will write notes for the support team, with most information remaining between the social worker and support team.",
      "cites": [5],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "If Jamie reports someone hurting him, the social worker may need to inform others to keep him safe, but will always tell him first.",
      "cites": [7],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie is attending college and does catering on Tuesdays and Wednesdays.",
      "cites": [10],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie volunteers at the garden centre on Fridays, doing watering and trolley duties.",
      "cites": [12],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie sometimes cooks for himself, but staff help with the oven.",
      "cites": [14],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie can cook pasta on his own.",
      "cites": [14],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sandra helps Jamie manage his shopping.",
      "cites": [16],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie receives money on a Monday and makes a shopping list.",
      "cites": [16],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie sees his mother on Sundays, who picks him up and they go to Nan's for dinner.",
      "cites": [18],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sandra and Priya are the staff Jamie gets on with best.",
      "cites": [20],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Craig is the night staff member most frequently assigned.",
      "cites": [22],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie gets on with Craig 'sometimes' and says he 'gets cross' when Jamie gets up at night.",
      "cites": [24, 26],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Craig tells Jamie to go back to bed when Jamie gets up at night for a drink.",
      "cites": [30],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Craig pushed Jamie into a wall in the hall outside the kitchen.",
      "cites": [34],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie's shoulder hurt when pushed into the wall.",
      "cites": [35],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "The incident when Craig pushed Jamie occurred on a Thursday night, the night before the garden centre.",
      "cites": [38, 40],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Craig kicked Jamie's leg with his foot on the back of his leg.",
      "cites": [46],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Craig kicked Jamie's leg three times, and said it was 'messing about' or a joke.",
      "cites": [48, 44],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie felt a bit of pain when kicked and had a bruise.",
      "cites": [50],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Craig told Jamie not to tell anyone about the kicking, saying if Jamie does, he will lose his flat.",
      "cites": [52],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie does not want to lose his flat.",
      "cites": [54],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jamie says Craig has not done anything else to him, but Marcus told him Craig hit Sophie, which Jamie did not see.",
      "cites": [58, 60],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "The social worker will report the incidents to the safeguarding team at the council.",
      "cites": [67],
      "section": "Agreed actions"
    },
    {
      "text": "The social worker will ring Sandra and the manager to ask that Craig does not work at night while the issue is being investigated.",
      "cites": [67],
      "section": "Agreed actions"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sandra will arrange alternative night staff if needed.",
      "cites": [69],
      "section": "Agreed actions"
    },
    {
      "text": "The social worker will contact Jamie's mother this afternoon.",
      "cites": [65],
      "section": "Agreed actions"
    },
    {
      "text": "A safeguarding team member may want to speak to Jamie, and the social worker will be present or his mother can be present.",
      "cites": [71],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "facts": [
    {
      "text": "Solicitor Helen Moss attended the meeting with client Gareth Pryce.",
      "cites": [1, 2],
      "section": "Attendance"
    },
    {
      "text": "The purpose of the meeting was to discuss Gareth Pryce's mother's estate, specifically the house on Wyvern Road.",
      "cites": [7],
      "section": "Attendance"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth Pryce's mother died in June.",
      "cites": [8],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "The house on Wyvern Road was left to Gareth and his brother Neil in equal shares, 50-50.",
      "cites": [8],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "There is a will naming both Gareth and Neil as executors.",
      "cites": [10],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Probate has not yet been applied for.",
      "cites": [11],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Neil is living in the house and refuses to move out.",
      "cites": [12],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "An estate agent provided an estimated valuation of £280,000 for the house.",
      "cites": [14],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Neil refused to allow a proper valuation by an estate agent.",
      "cites": [14],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth and Neil have a strained relationship, described as 'bad' or 'really bad'.",
      "cites": [16],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "On Saturday, 7th November, Neil punched Gareth in the face during an argument in the kitchen about the sale of the house.",
      "cites": [24, 26, 27, 32],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth's nose was broken during the incident, and he was taken to hospital that night.",
      "cites": [29, 31],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth was treated at Castlebrook General Hospital A and E, where an x-ray confirmed a broken nose.",
      "cites": [31],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "After being punched, Gareth was on the floor and was hit in the back and shoulder with a kitchen chair.",
      "cites": [33, 35],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth had bruising down his back for a week following the incident.",
      "cites": [35],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth stated that Neil was 'like a different person' during the incident.",
      "cites": [37],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth said he did not believe Neil had a knife or picked one up during the incident, but that he was angry and it scared him.",
      "cites": [38, 40],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth left the house after getting up and walking out, then drove himself to hospital.",
      "cites": [42],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth has not reported the incident to the police.",
      "cites": [43],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth said he is thinking about reporting the incident to the police, but is concerned about his mother's feelings.",
      "cites": [44],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth has a discharge letter from Castlebrook General Hospital.",
      "cites": [46],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth took photos of his face the day after the incident.",
      "cites": [46],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Neil has sent texts to Gareth, saying he 'deserved it' and that he is not getting a penny.",
      "cites": [48],
      "section": "Client's account"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth wants the house sold and the estate settled.",
      "cites": [52],
      "section": "Client's objectives"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gareth wants Neil to stay away from him.",
      "cites": [52],
      "section": "Client's objectives"
    },
    {
      "text": "As joint executors, both Gareth and Neil must act to apply for probate, but if Neil refuses to cooperate, the solicitor advised that a court application to remove Neil as an execu­",
      "cites": [53],
      "section": "Advice given"
    },
    {
      "text": "The solicitor advised that a letter to Neil should be written, setting out a deadline, and that Gareth should consider reporting the assault to the police.",
      "cites": [55],
      "section": "Advice given"
    },
    {
      "text": "The solicitor advised that a non-molestation order could be applied for in family court to prevent Neil from contacting or approaching Gareth.",
      "cites": [57],
      "section": "Advice given"
    },
    {
      "text": "The solicitor stated that a non-molestation order could be processed quickly if urgent.",
      "cites": [59],
      "section": "Advice given"
    },
    {
      "text": "The solicitor will send a client care letter with fees by Friday.",
      "cites": [61],
      "section": "Advice given"
    } ]}

{
  "facts": [
    {
      "text": "Leanne Marsh is the person being assessed.",
      "cites": [2],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The assessment is Leanne's review.",
      "cites": [2],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The person is currently living with her mother.",
      "cites": [12],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "The person's mother has bad knees.",
      "cites": [12],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Leanne helps her mother with hoovering.",
      "cites": [12],
      "section": "Background and presenting situation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Leanne enjoys art and is working on a large painting of her cat Biscuit.",
      "cites": [8],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Leanne enjoys cooking on Mondays.",
      "cites": [10],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Leanne enjoys the disco on Fridays.",
      "cites": [10],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Leanne currently travels to the service via minibus.",
      "cites": [16],
      "section": "Needs and daily living"
    },
    {
      "text": "Leanne does not like Dave, the driver of the minibus.",
      "cites": [20],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dave touches Leanne on her chest on the minibus.",
      "cites": [26, 28],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dave touches Leanne between her legs over her trousers on the minibus.",
      "cites": [32],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dave kisses Leanne on her mouth.",
      "cites": [40],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dave says it is a 'secret' between them and does not want Leanne to tell her mother.",
      "cites": [42],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "These incidents occur every week when Leanne is the last person to get off the minibus.",
      "cites": [44, 46],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "The incidents started after Leanne's birthday in August.",
      "cites": [48],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Leanne denies that the incidents were stories and confirms they are true.",
      "cites": [34, 38],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "No staff at Brookside have touched Leanne in a similar way.",
      "cites": [50, 52],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "The social worker will inform the safeguarding team at the council and the police about the incidents.",
      "cites": [57],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "The social worker will ensure Leanne is accompanied if police or safeguarding staff speak to her.",
      "cites": [59],
      "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
    },
    {
      "text": "Leanne will not be travelling on Dave's minibus from tomorrow.",
      "cites": [65],
      "section": "Agreed actions"
    },
    {
      "text": "Leanne requests a taxi instead of her mother driving.",
      "cites": [66],
      "section": "Agreed actions"
    },
    {
      "text": "The social worker will contact the centre manager Joanne to arrange a taxi from Wednesday onwards.",
      "cites": [67],
      "section": "Agreed actions"
    },
    {
      "text": "The social worker will visit Leanne's house tomorrow at 4 o'clock to inform her mother together.",
      "cites": [69],
