{ "facts": [
  {
    "text": "Solicitor Daniel Okafor attended the meeting with client Rachel Penrose.",
    "cites": [1, 2],
    "section": "Attendance"
  },
  {
    "text": "The purpose of the meeting was for Rachel Penrose to disclose information about her mother Margaret's financial and care situation, including concerns about her brother Martin's un","cites": [10, 11, 12, 13, 14],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Margaret Penrose is 81 years old and has been diagnosed with dementia since two years ago.",
    "cites": [11],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Margaret Penrose lives at 81 Larch Road with carers.",
    "cites": [11],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Martin Penrose holds the power of attorney for financial and property matters for Margaret Penrose.",
    "cites": [13],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The power of attorney was signed by Margaret Penrose in 2023 and was registered.",
    "cites": [13],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Martin Penrose is the sole attorney; Rachel Penrose is not an attorney.",
    "cites": [14, 15],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "On 14 August, a transfer of £12,000 was made from Margaret Penrose's account to Martin Penrose's account.",
    "cites": [17, 19],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The transfer was to an account in Martin Penrose's name, as indicated by the account numbers.",
    "cites": [19],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose took photos of the bank statement on 14 August and printed them for reference.",
    "cites": [21],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "On 22 September, Margaret Penrose told Rachel Penrose that Martin had made her sign a document without her understanding.",
    "cites": [29, 31, 32],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Margaret Penrose did not know what the document was or what it was for.",
    "cites": [31, 35],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose has not seen the document that Margaret signed on 22 September.",
    "cites": [33, 35],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Brightwell care agency sent a letter dated 3 November stating that invoices are three months overdue and that they may stop calls if unpaid.",
    "cites": [39, 41],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The outstanding care bills amount to approximately £2,400.",
    "cites": [39],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose has the letter from Brightwell dated 3 November.",
    "cites": [41],
    "section": "Documents and evidence"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose has photos of the bank statement showing the £12,000 transfer on 14 August.",
    "cites": [21],
    "section": "Documents and evidence"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose has not provided any document related to the document signed by her mother on 22 September.",
    "cites": [33, 35],
    "section": "Documents and evidence"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose wants to protect her mother's money and prevent Martin from accessing it.",
    "cites": [45],
    "section": "Client's objectives"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose is concerned that if Martin sells the house, there will be nothing left for her mother's care.",
    "cites": [47, 48],
    "section": "Client's objectives"
  },
  {
    "text": "Martin Penrose has not said anything about selling the house, nor has it been put on the market.",
    "cites": [48, 49],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor advised that a transfer of £12,000 by an attorney without authority may be investigated by the Office of the Public Guardian.",
    "cites": [50],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The Office of the Public Guardian supervises attorneys and can request Martin to account for every penny of the transfer.",
    "cites": [52],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The Office of the Public Guardian can apply to the Court of Protection to cancel the power of attorney if necessary.",
    "cites": [52],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor advised that taking money as an attorney without proper authority may be a criminal offence.",
    "cites": [54],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor advised that an adult safeguarding referral to Wexley Council is appropriate due to Margaret Penrose being an adult at risk.",
    "cites": [55, 56],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor advised that Rachel Penrose should not confront Martin about the financial matters at this time to avoid him moving money or becoming defensive.",
    "cites": [58, 59],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose will call Brightwell care agency tomorrow to explain that the bills are in hand and to prevent service interruption.",
    "cites": [61],
    "section": "Next steps"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose will email the solicitor the photos of the bank statement and the Brightwell letter by Friday, 27 November.",
    "cites": [62],
    "section": "Next steps"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor will write to the Office of the Public Guardian by Tuesday, 1 December.",
    "cites": [62],
    "section": "Next steps"
  } ]}

