{ "facts": [
  {
    "text": "Amina Hussain is the health visitor conducting Leo and Poppy's two-year review.",
    "cites": [5, 10, 11, 12, 13],
    "section": "Background and presenting situation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade Turner is the mother of Leo and Poppy.",
    "cites": [2, 5, 10, 11, 12],
    "section": "Background and presenting situation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Leo is two years old and Poppy is five months old.",
    "cites": [5, 10, 11, 12],
    "section": "Background and presenting situation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Leo can say about twenty words, including 'mama', 'car', 'more', 'bye-bye', and 'dog'.",
    "cites": [8],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Leo is able to put two words together, such as 'more juice'.",
    "cites": [10],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Leo is active and runs and climbs, having climbed the bookcase last week.",
    "cites": [11, 12],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Leo's eating habits are fussy, with preferences for toast, pasta, and yoghurt.",
    "cites": [14],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Poppy is fed with bottles, approximately six per day, and has started on baby rice.",
    "cites": [16],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Poppy has a nappy rash that is severe, with broken skin, and has lasted about a week.",
    "cites": [17, 18, 20],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade has been applying Sudocrem to Poppy's nappy rash.",
    "cites": [18],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade has run out of nappies on Sunday and has been leaving them on longer.",
    "cites": [18],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade has only one tin of Poppy's milk left, which will last until Friday.",
    "cites": [22],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "The milk supply will last until Friday, when Jade's Universal Credit payment comes in.",
    "cites": [23, 24],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade has a cleaning job at a retail park, working nights from ten to twelve, sometimes half past twelve.",
    "cites": [26, 27, 28],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade's cleaning job is cash in hand.",
    "cites": [26],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade's friend Shannon looks after Leo and Poppy while she is at work, but Shannon cannot always do so.",
    "cites": [30],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "When Shannon cannot look after the children, Jade leaves them alone for a couple of hours, while they are asleep and do not wake up.",
    "cites": [32, 34],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade leaves the children alone for about three nights a week, since Shannon started her new job, over the last month.",
    "cites": [38, 39],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade is concerned that if she loses her cleaning job, she and her children will be evicted.",
    "cites": [44],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade has not received any letters from the landlord or notices of eviction.",
    "cites": [45, 46],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade has not applied for nursery for Leo, who is two years old and eligible for 15 hours of funded nursery.",
    "cites": [53, 54],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Little Acorns nursery on Marlow Road has spaces available from January and is recommended for Leo.",
    "cites": [55],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade will not leave Leo and Poppy alone if Shannon cannot have them, and will text her supervisor to state she has no childcare.",
    "cites": [57, 58],
    "section": "Agreed actions"
  },
  {
    "text": "Amina will make a referral to children's social care to support childcare arrangements.",
    "cites": [43, 57],
    "section": "Agreed actions"
  },
  {
    "text": "Amina will drop a food bank voucher at the household before 3pm today.",
    "cites": [59],
    "section": "Agreed actions"
  },
  {
    "text": "Amina will book Poppy in with Dr Lowe for a nappy rash assessment tomorrow.",
    "cites": [61],
    "section": "Agreed actions"
  },
  {
    "text": "Amina will bring nappies to the household when she returns to see Poppy.",
    "cites": [61],
    "section": "Agreed actions"
  },
  {
    "text": "Amina will return to the household on Monday the 30th at 10am to support with the nursery form and check on the family's well-being.",
    "cites": [63, 64],
    "section": "Agreed actions"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade's mother is in Northby and would help if she were to contact her, but they are not currently in contact.",
    "cites": [50, 51],
    "section": "Support network and finances"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade is worried that if something happens to Leo or Poppy—such as a fire or Poppy choking—there would be no one to help them, and this is a concern for the health visitor.",
    "cites": [41],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  }
] }

{ "facts": [
  {
    "text": "Siobhan Kelly is the district nurse who has been seeing Keith Dawson for leg ulcers.",
    "cites": [10],
    "section": "Background and presenting situation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson has leg ulcers on both legs that are slow to heal.",
    "cites": [10],
    "section": "Background and presenting situation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson has not had heating since October.",
    "cites": [12],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson has not had hot water since October.",
    "cites": [14],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson has been using a fan heater but finds it expensive and does not use it regularly.",
    "cites": [14],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson has not washed in three to four weeks.",
    "cites": [20],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson has not cooked meals for himself due to the absence of hot water and the presence of rats in the kitchen.",
    "cites": [24, 28],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson has seen two rats in the kitchen, which have been feeding on bread, and has stopped using the kitchen for food storage.",
    "cites": [24, 26],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson has not had meals for four days last week due to missed home care visits.",
    "cites": [35, 36],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "The home care agency Bright Days was supposed to provide morning and teatime visits.",
    "cites": [30],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "In the last two weeks, Bright Days missed 16 out of 28 scheduled visits, with no record of visits for 16 days.",
    "cites": [33],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "For four consecutive days last week, no one from Bright Days came to visit Keith Dawson.",
    "cites": [35],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson did not contact Bright Days when visits were missed, stating he did not want to bother them.",
    "cites": [36],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "The neighbour at number 25 reported to the district nurse that Keith Dawson has been drinking heavily.",
    "cites": [38],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "The district nurse Siobhan Kelly did not personally observe any signs of Keith Dawson drinking heavily.",
    "cites": [40],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson denies the claim about heavy drinking and calls the neighbour a 'nosy cow'.",
    "cites": [42],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson's GP is Dr Morgan at Holloway surgery.",
    "cites": [44],
    "section": "Background and presenting situation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson has not seen his wife since 2015.",
    "cites": [46],
    "section": "Background and presenting situation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson's brother Phil lives in Northby and they only communicate at Christmas.",
    "cites": [46],
    "section": "Background and presenting situation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson receives Employment and Support Allowance (ESA) and is waiting for a pension to start next year.",
    "cites": [48],
    "section": "Background and presenting situation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson believes he is up to date with his bills, though the gas is on a meter.",
    "cites": [50],
    "section": "Background and presenting situation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson's primary wish is for the heating to be fixed and the rats to be removed.",
    "cites": [52],
    "section": "Person's views and wishes"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson stated he does not want a home or any form of relocation.",
    "cites": [52],
    "section": "Person's views and wishes"
  },
  {
    "text": "The social worker Rachel Burns will raise a safeguarding concern about the missed care visits and the poor condition of the home.",
    "cites": [53],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Keith Dawson agrees to a safeguarding concern being raised if the boiler is fixed.",
    "cites": [54],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "The social worker will contact the housing association to log the boiler as an emergency repair.",
    "cites": [55],
    "section": "Agreed actions"
  },
  {
    "text": "The social worker will request two oil heaters to be delivered to the home within the next 24 hours.",
    "cites": [55],
    "section": "Agreed actions"
  },
  {
    "text": "The social worker will contact environmental health to arrange pest control in the kitchen.",
    "cites": [57],
    "section": "Agreed actions"
  },
  {
    "text": "The social worker will raise the issue of missed visits with Bright Days and the commissioning team.",
    "cites": [57],
    "section": "Agreed actions"
  },
  {
    "text": "The district nurse will continue to visit Keith Dawson on Tuesdays and Fridays for leg ulcer care.",
    "cites": [58],
    "section": "Support network and finances"
  } ] }

{ "facts": [
  {
    "text": "Social worker Priya Nandra is conducting a review following Edna Hollis's fall in October.",
    "cites": [5, 15],
    "section": "Background and presenting situation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna Hollis has a hip injury that causes stiffness in the mornings and limits mobility.",
    "cites": [9, 10],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna Hollis uses a frame in the house for mobility support.",
    "cites": [10],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna Hollis does not go out without someone accompanying her.",
    "cites": [10],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Carers visit Edna Hollis in the morning and at teatime.",
    "cites": [11, 14],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "The morning carer is named Jade.",
    "cites": [12],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Jade helps Edna Hollis with medication and personal washing.",
    "cites": [12],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Teatime carers arrive quickly but are often in and out, which Edna describes as 'a bit quick sometimes'.",
    "cites": [14],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna's daughter Sandra shops for her once a week on a Saturday.",
    "cites": [16],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Sandra lives in Castleford and drives to visit Edna.",
    "cites": [16],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna's grandson Kyle visits most weeks.",
    "cites": [18],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Kyle brings Edna's newspapers and goes to the cash machine for her because she can't access the post office.",
    "cites": [20],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Kyle uses Edna's bank card to access money.",
    "cites": [22],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna gave Kyle her bank card number to make it easier.",
    "cites": [22],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Kyle takes out £50 per week from Edna's bank card for himself.",
    "cites": [24],
    "section": "Needs and daily living"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna did not agree to Kyle taking £50 per week; she did not consent to this arrangement.",
    "cites": [28],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna did not authorize Kyle to take £50 per week; the money was taken without her explicit consent.",
    "cites": [28],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna reported that Kyle took £400 from her purse three weeks ago, after a visit.",
    "cites": [32, 33, 36],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "The £400 was in Edna's purse and was gone after Kyle visited.",
    "cites": [33],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Kyle said he was only borrowing the £400 and would repay it, stating it was not stealing from his grandmother.",
    "cites": [34],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Kyle has not repaid the £400 as of the date of the conversation.",
    "cites": [36],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Sandra told Edna that Kyle gambles on his phone using betting apps.",
    "cites": [46],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna has not personally seen Kyle gambling or accessed his phone to verify the gambling activity.",
    "cites": [48],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Sandra knows about the £400 incident in the purse but does not know about the weekly £50 withdrawals.",
    "cites": [50],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna does not believe Kyle has threatened or harmed her physically or emotionally.",
    "cites": [44],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna does not want Kyle to be involved with police or legal action.",
    "cites": [52],
    "section": "Person's views and wishes"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna wants her money to be her own and does not want it to be taken by Kyle.",
    "cites": [52],
    "section": "Person's views and wishes"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edna does not want the police involved in the matter involving Kyle and her money.",
    "cites": [55],
    "section": "Person's views and wishes"
  },
  {
    "text": "The social worker will log a safeguarding concern due to money being taken by Kyle without consent.",
    "cites": [54],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  },
  {
    "text": "The safeguarding concern will be logged with the team, not with the police.",
    "cites": [54],
    "section": "Risks and safeguarding"
  } ]}

{ "facts": [
  {
    "text": "Solicitor Daniel Okafor attended the meeting with client Rachel Penrose.",
    "cites": [1],
    "section": "Attendance"
  },
  {
    "text": "The purpose of the meeting was for Rachel Penrose to disclose concerns about her mother Margaret's financial and care situation, particularly regarding her brother Martin's actions",
    "cites": [10],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose described her mother Margaret as 81 years old, diagnosed with dementia two years ago, and still living in her own house on Larch Road with carers.",
    "cites": [11],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose's brother Martin holds the power of attorney for financial matters (money, property and financial affairs) for her mother, which was signed in 2023 and registered.",
    "cites": [13],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Only Martin holds the power of attorney; Rachel Penrose does not have a co-attorney.",
    "cites": [14],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose discovered a bank transfer of £12,000 from her mother's account to Martin's account on 14 August.",
    "cites": [17, 19],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The transfer was to Martin's account, as confirmed by the account number ending in the last digits of Martin's account.",
    "cites": [19],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose saw her mother on 22 September, when her mother said, 'Martin made me sign something' and that Martin put it in front of her and made her sign it, and she was afraid",
    "cites": [29, 31, 32],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose did not see or have access to the document her mother referred to, and has searched her mother's drawers without finding it.",
    "cites": [35, 36],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The care agency Brightwell sent a letter dated 3 November stating that invoices are three months overdue and amount to approximately £2,400, and that they may stop calls if unpaid.",
    "cites": [39, 41],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose has the letter from Brightwell dated 3 November, which she will provide to the solicitor.",
    "cites": [41],
    "section": "Documents and evidence"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose has photos of the bank statement showing the £12,000 transfer on 14 August, which she printed and brought to the meeting.",
    "cites": [21, 22],
    "section": "Documents and evidence"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose stated her objective is to protect her mother's money and prevent Martin from accessing it, and to ensure the house is not sold, as that would leave nothing for her母",
    "cites": [45, 47],
    "section": "Client's objectives"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose expressed concern that if Martin sells the house, there will be nothing left for her mother's care, which keeps her awake.",
    "cites": [47],
    "section": "Client's objectives"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose stated Martin has not said anything about selling the house, and she is only worried he might do so.",
    "cites": [48, 49],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor advised that an attorney must act in the client's best interests and keep her money separate, and that a transfer of £12,000 without authority is something the Office",
    "cites": [50],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The Office of the Public Guardian supervises attorneys and can investigate the transfer, require Martin to account for every penny, and apply to the Court of Protection to cancel a",
    "cites": [52],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor advised that taking money as an attorney without proper authority may be a criminal offence.",
    "cites": [54],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor recommended a safeguarding referral to Wexley Council because the client's mother is an adult at risk.",
    "cites": [55, 56],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose agreed to the safeguarding referral being made by the solicitor.",
    "cites": [57],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor advised Rachel Penrose not to confront Martin about the transfer or the document at this time, as it could cause him to move money or become defensive.",
    "cites": [58, 59],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose agreed to call Brightwell to explain the situation and confirm payment of the invoices, and will do so tomorrow.",
    "cites": [61],
    "section": "Next steps"
  },
  {
    "text": "Rachel Penrose will email the solicitor the photos of the bank statement and the Brightwell letter by Friday, 27th of November.",
