{ "facts": [
  {
    "text": "Solicitor Sophie Grant attended the meeting with client Lee Whitfield.",
    "cites": [1, 2],
    "section": "Attendance"
  },
  {
    "text": "The purpose of the meeting was to discuss the client's housing situation, including rent arrears and court proceedings.",
    "cites": [5],
    "section": "Attendance"
  },
  {
    "text": "Client Lee Whitfield lost his job at a depot in January.",
    "cites": [6],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client's Universal Credit housing element took a long time to process, and the housing element went wrong, leading to rent arrears.",
    "cites": [6],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The rent arrears amount is £3,850, for three to four months.",
    "cites": [8],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client received court papers for a possession claim on rent arrears grounds (grounds 8, 10, and 11) by Ashcroft Lettings.",
    "cites": [10, 11],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The hearing is scheduled for the 9th of December at Harbridge County Court.",
    "cites": [10],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The property is a private rental property.",
    "cites": [11],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client lives alone with a cat.",
    "cites": [14],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client offered £50 per month in September to settle the arrears, which the landlord rejected.",
    "cites": [16],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client has a text message recording the offer of £50 per month, which is stored on their phone.",
    "cites": [18],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client reported damp in the bedroom, with black mould on the wall.",
    "cites": [20],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client has photographs of the damp in the bedroom.",
    "cites": [20],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client has outstanding debts including council tax (bailiffs letter sent), a credit card debt of approximately £2,000, and electric bill on a meter.",
    "cites": [22],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client has no support from family or friends, with only a brother in Doncaster who does not communicate regularly.",
    "cites": [27, 28],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client visited his GP in March after receiving the first rent arrears letter.",
    "cites": [28],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client took an overdose of 16 paracetamol in March after receiving the first rent arrears letter.",
    "cites": [32, 34],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client's neighbour found him and called an ambulance, and he was admitted overnight to hospital.",
    "cites": [34],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "After hospital admission, a nurse contacted the client a couple of times, then stopped contacting.",
    "cites": [36],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client has not hurt himself since March.",
    "cites": [38],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client thought about ending his life on Sunday night, this week, before the court date.",
    "cites": [40, 44],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client is currently safe and stable today.",
    "cites": [46],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client stated that talking about the suicidal thoughts helped him feel a bit better.",
    "cites": [46],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor advised the client that the arrears are due to the housing element going wrong, and that the damp may be a valid counterclaim to reduce the arrears.",
    "cites": [51],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor will file a defence and a counterclaim for damp issues.",
    "cites": [51],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor will request the court to adjourn if more time is needed to resolve the Universal Credit issue.",
    "cites": [53],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor will refer the client to the Citizens Advice debt team for a breathing space (60-day period during which creditors do not chase the client).",
    "cites": [55],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The client reported that he had previously submitted issues with the housing costs to the Universal Credit journal twice, but received no response.",
    "cites": [58],
    "section": "Client's account"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor will write to Universal Credit to support the defence of the housing claim.",
    "cites": [59],
    "section": "Advice given"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solicitor requires the following documents: tenancy agreement, rent statement, Universal Credit statements since January, and damp photos.",
    "cites": [60],
    "section": "Documents and evidence"
  } ]}

